== Notes ==
* In the boss room, Monstro can be paired with {{e|Fly|text=Flies}}, {{e|Attack Fly|text=Attack Flies}}, {{e|Gaper}}s, {{e|Hopper}}s, {{e|Frowning Gaper}}s, {{e|Mulligan}}s, {{e|Cyclopia}}s, or {{e|Ministro}}s.
* When Monstro jumps off-screen, he is cured of all status effects.
* {{dlc|nr}} Monstro can't hop over [[Obstacles]].
* Larger [[Tears]] that Monstro shoots deal 1 [[Heart]] of damage, while the smaller [[Tears]] only deal half a [[Heart]] of damage.
** If Isaac is somewhere that Monstro cannot reach, Monstro will jump in place.
** If Isaac has flight and is over an obstacle, Monstro will essentially be unable to perform any attacks.
*** While Monstro can hit Isaac with his tear barrage because of its tear height, it is very unlikely.
* {{dlc|a+}} Monstro can rarely spawn in a room with two {{M|Blood Donation Machine}}s.


== Trivia ==
* Monstro appeared in the original ''The Binding of Isaac.''
* He is the boss version of the {{e|Ministro}}s.
* Monstro appears to be missing a tooth which appears as the item, {{i|Monstro's Tooth}}.
** Monstro also has a [[wikipedia:Cleft lip and palate|cleft lip]].
* Monstro is ''Monster'' in Portuguese.
** "Monstro" is a somewhat common mispronunciation of the Spanish word ''monstruo''.
** Monstro is also the name of [[Wikipedia:The Terrible Dogfish|The Terrible Dogfish]], a fish with a large mouth and many teeth from the book ''[[Wikipedia:The Adventures of Pinocchio|The Adventures of Pinocchio]]''.

